      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "tape",
      "description": "Label-maker tape for section labels and status; solid for released, outline for not yet proven.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-plate\"><span class=\"ds-tape\"><span class=\"ds-led ds-led-g\"></span>v1.9.0 · Released</span><span class=\"ds-tape ds-tape-outline\"><span class=\"ds-led ds-led-a\"></span>v0.9.0 · Prerelease · Offline-proven</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-plate{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;padding:18px;background:#1E2125;color:#EEF1F3}.ds-tape{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.55em;padding:.5em .75em .45em;border-radius:2px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.28),rgba(255,255,255,0) 45%),var(--tape,#F2D024);color:var(--tape-ink,#121417);font-family:Archivo,'Arial Narrow',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.75rem;font-stretch:75%;font-weight:750;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;box-shadow:0 1px 1px rgba(0,0,0,.3),0 3px 8px -2px rgba(0,0,0,.25)}.ds-tape-outline{background:transparent;color:#EEF1F3;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--tape,#F2D024)}.ds-led{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%}.ds-led-g{background:radial-gradient(circle at 35% 35%,#C9F7D4 0 18%,#33C25A 55%);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,.3),0 0 7px 1px rgba(51,194,90,.55)}.ds-led-a{background:radial-gradient(circle at 35% 35%,#FFE2B8 0 18%,#FF9F1A 55%);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,.3),0 0 7px 1px rgba(255,159,26,.55);animation:ds-blink 2.4s steps(1,end) infinite}@keyframes ds-blink{0%,62%{opacity:1}63%,100%{opacity:.25}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-led-a{animation:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Top-of-Rack Switch Nav",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "port",
      "description": "1U switch; each nav link is an RJ45 port whose link LED lights on hover or when active.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-switch\" aria-label=\"Primary\"><span class=\"ds-sw-name\">Mike Dopp</span><a class=\"ds-port is-active\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-jack\"><span class=\"ds-pled\"></span></span>Work</a><a class=\"ds-port\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-jack\"><span class=\"ds-pled\"></span></span>Skills</a><a class=\"ds-port\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-jack\"><span class=\"ds-pled\"></span></span>Contact</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-switch{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;min-height:48px;padding:0 24px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#1E2125,#17191C);color:#EEF1F3;font-family:Archivo,'Arial Narrow',system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-sw-name{margin-right:auto;font-size:.875rem;font-stretch:125%;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-port{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:40px;padding:0 10px 0 6px;border-radius:3px;color:#EEF1F3;font-size:.75rem;font-stretch:80%;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none;transition:background-color 160ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}.ds-port:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.07)}.ds-port:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #F2D024;outline-offset:3px}.ds-jack{position:relative;width:22px;height:18px;border-radius:2px;background:#07080A;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px #3A4148}.ds-pled{position:absolute;top:3px;right:3px;width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:1px;background:#474E55;transition:background-color 200ms,box-shadow 200ms}.ds-port:hover .ds-pled,.ds-port.is-active .ds-pled{background:#33C25A;box-shadow:0 0 5px 1px rgba(51,194,90,.6)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Pull Handle",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "handle",
      "description": "Opens a server unit's service view; the chevron flips when expanded.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-fp\"><button class=\"ds-handle\" type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><span class=\"ds-grip\"></span>Service view<svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m4 6 4 4 4-4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-fp{padding:18px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#1E2125,#17191C);color:#EEF1F3}.ds-handle{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:44px;padding:0 14px 0 10px;border:0;border-radius:10px;background:transparent;color:#EEF1F3;font-family:Archivo,'Arial Narrow',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.8125rem;font-stretch:85%;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;cursor:pointer;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px #8A939B;transition:box-shadow 160ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1),background-color 160ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}.ds-handle:hover{background:rgba(127,136,144,.14);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px #EEF1F3}.ds-handle:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #F2D024;outline-offset:3px}.ds-handle svg{transition:transform 420ms cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)}.ds-handle[aria-expanded=\"true\"] svg{transform:rotate(180deg)}.ds-grip{width:4px;height:22px;border-radius:2px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(180deg,currentColor 0 2px,transparent 2px 4px);opacity:.6}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Silver 1U Link Unit",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "button-steel",
      "description": "A 1U link unit on the silver finish with corner screws; the container pattern used instead of cards.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-unit\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-u-name\">GitHub repositories</span><span class=\"ds-u-desc\">Everything public.</span></a>",
      "css": ".ds-unit{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;min-height:47px;padding:8px 40px;border-top:1px solid #07080A;background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(255,255,255,.07) 0 1px,transparent 1px 3px),linear-gradient(180deg,#E3E7EA 0%,#CDD3D7 55%,#C3CACF 100%);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 #F5F7F8,inset 0 -2px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.12);color:#121417;font-family:Archivo,'Arial Narrow',system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none}.ds-unit::before{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;background:radial-gradient(circle,#A3ACB3 0 3px,#5F676E 3.6px 4.6px,transparent 5.2px) 5px 50%/14px 14px no-repeat,radial-gradient(circle,#A3ACB3 0 3px,#5F676E 3.6px 4.6px,transparent 5.2px) calc(100% - 5px) 50%/14px 14px no-repeat}.ds-u-name{font-size:.9375rem;font-stretch:115%;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.03em;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-u-desc{color:#39414A;font-size:.9375rem}.ds-unit:hover .ds-u-name{text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:.25em}.ds-unit:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #121417;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Spec Sticker",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "spec-sticker",
      "description": "A stuck-on spec line inside the dark service tray.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tray\"><p class=\"ds-sticker\">Plans with SHA-256 before anything is written.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tray{padding:22px;background:#121417}.ds-sticker{margin:0;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:3px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#EEF1F3,#DCE1E4);color:#121417;font-family:Archivo,'Arial Narrow',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.42;box-shadow:0 1px 1px rgba(0,0,0,.5),0 4px 10px -6px rgba(0,0,0,.6)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Patch Panel Port",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "tape",
      "description": "A skill as a labelled port: patched (yellow boot, green LED). The panel shows production skills only.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-pp-row\"><span class=\"ds-pp\"><span class=\"ds-pp-l\">PowerShell</span><span class=\"ds-pp-j ds-patched\"><span class=\"ds-pp-led\"></span></span></span><span class=\"ds-pp\"><span class=\"ds-pp-l\">vSphere</span><span class=\"ds-pp-j ds-patched\"><span class=\"ds-pp-led\"></span></span></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-pp-row{display:flex;gap:10px;padding:18px;background:#1E2125;color:#EEF1F3;font-family:Archivo,'Arial Narrow',system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-pp{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:96px}.ds-pp-l{width:100%;padding:6px 4px;border-radius:2px;background:#F2D024;color:#121417;font-size:.75rem;font-stretch:70%;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.02em;text-align:center;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-pp-j{position:relative;width:34px;height:28px;border-radius:3px;background:#050607;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px #343A40}.ds-patched::after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:3px 4px 2px;border-radius:3px 3px 5px 5px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#F7DB45,#D9B70C);box-shadow:0 2px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.55)}.ds-pp-led{position:absolute;z-index:1;top:-1px;right:-1px;width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:#33C25A;box-shadow:0 0 0 1px #050607,0 0 5px 1px rgba(51,194,90,.55)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Rack Elevation",
    "overview": "The site is a technical drawing of one server rack seen from the front. A cool light-gray drafting sheet, framed by a hairline border and a heavy outer rule, carries a dimension line across the top and a title block at the bottom right. On the sheet stands a single graphite rack with cage-nut rails and U numbers; every piece of content is a unit bolted into it. Navigation is a 1U top-of-rack switch whose ports are the links, the introduction is a 4U appliance with a silver faceplate, projects are 3U servers that slide out on rails into a service view, skills are a patch panel, the about text sits on a KVM console drawer, contact is a PDU, and empty space is a blanking panel.\n\nThe world is dense, physical and literal. Everything is rendered as an object with an edge, a screw, a seam or a label, and nothing floats free of the rack. The palette is restricted to the inks such a rack actually has: steel in many tones, label-maker yellow tape, and LED states. Type does its work through Archivo's width axis: wide uppercase nameplates for model names and condensed caps for tape labels, with Martian Mono reserved for machine data.\n\nState is shown as a mark with words beside it, never as colour alone. A released unit carries solid tape and a steady green LED; an unproven one carries hairline-outline tape and a blinking amber LED, and its text says what has not been proven.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One rack, stacked units with no gaps between them; vertical rhythm in 48px rack units.",
      "Restricted inks: sheet gray, steel, tape yellow, LED green and amber.",
      "Archivo's width axis carries hierarchy (wide nameplates, condensed labels).",
      "Martian Mono only for data: U numbers, asset IDs, LED codes, dates, ratings.",
      "Physical depth: inset bevels on faceplates, small cast shadows on objects that sit proud (tape, stickers, buttons, tags).",
      "One signature motion: a server unit slides out on its rails; LEDs blink. Both stop under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Restricted Inks Rule",
        "body": "Steel, tape yellow and the two LED colours are the whole palette. No blue links, no brand gradients, no second accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State Is a Mark Rule",
        "body": "An LED or tape style never carries state alone. The state is always written next to it (\"v0.9.0 · Prerelease · Offline-proven\", \"Accepting interviews\"), and an unproven state uses outline tape plus amber, a released one solid tape plus green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Yellow Is a Label Rule",
        "body": "Yellow appears only where a real rack would have tape or a coloured part (labels, cable boots, the live outlet, the one primary button). It is never a background wash or a decorative stripe.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Width Axis Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from width before size: wide (125) for things that are named, condensed (70–90) for things that are labelled. Never set a nameplate condensed or a tape label wide.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is Data Rule",
        "body": "Martian Mono is for identifiers, numbers and codes that a machine would print. Sentences are never set in mono.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The U Rule",
        "body": "Vertical rhythm is the 48px rack unit. Content is added as another unit in the stack, not as a free-floating card with margins around it.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Proud Object Rule",
        "body": "A cast shadow means the thing is physically on top of the faceplate (tape, sticker, tag, button, plug) or has been pulled out. Faceplates themselves only get bevels.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do add new content as a rack unit with a finish class (silver, graphite or black), stacked edge to edge with the 1px seam.",
      "Do label sections with tape on a cable manager, and write every status in words next to its LED or tape style.",
      "Do use outline tape plus amber for anything not yet proven, and solid tape plus green only for released, proven work.",
      "Do set names in wide Archivo caps (wdth 125, 800) and labels in condensed Archivo caps (wdth 70–90, 650–750).",
      "Do keep Martian Mono to identifiers, numbers and codes.",
      "Do keep motion to the rail slide and LED behaviour, and make both steady under reduced motion.",
      "Do use the Rack Black focus ring on light surfaces and the tape-yellow ring on dark steel."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce a hue outside steel, tape yellow and the two LED colours.",
      "Don't let an LED colour or tape style be the only carrier of a state.",
      "Don't float content in rounded cards with gaps between them; the rack is continuous.",
      "Don't put cast shadows on faceplates at rest; shadows belong to objects sitting on them or a pulled unit.",
      "Don't use yellow as a background fill for a whole unit or as decoration.",
      "Don't set sentences in Martian Mono or nameplates in condensed widths.",
      "Don't round corners beyond 6px, except the 10px pull handle and circular LEDs."
    ]
  }
}